cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  Cite the archived v1.1.0 release using the version-specific Zenodo DOI below.
  For development changes after this release, also report the Git commit used.
type: software
title: >-
  Replication Materials for "Voting Patterns, Mortality, and Health Inequalities
  in England: A replication and extension of Smith and Dorling (1996)"
authors:
  - family-names: Rahal
    given-names: Charles
    affiliation: University of Oxford
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23690243
version: v1.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-27
repository-code: https://github.com/crahal/voting_mortality_inequality
url: https://zenodo.org/records/23690243
abstract: >-
  Replication code and publication outputs for an ecological analysis of voting,
  mortality and health inequalities across English parliamentary constituencies.
  Includes 2019 and 2024 election analyses, 2021 premature mortality compared
  with 2019 voting, and regional and spatial sensitivity analyses. Public source
  inputs are downloaded and checked against pinned checksums; raw inputs are
  not redistributed in this archive.
keywords:
  - health inequalities
  - mortality
  - elections
  - England
  - reproducible research
